---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '10 August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — WP Base"
  description="How WP Base collects, uses and protects your personal information."
>
  <main class="legal">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <p>
        This policy explains what personal information WP Base collects, why it
        is collected, and what you can do about it. It is written in plain
        English rather than legal boilerplate, and it covers this website,
        enquiry forms, email correspondence and any paid care plans.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Who is responsible for your information</h2>
      <p>
        WP Base is a WordPress maintenance and web design business run by Chris
        Kernaghan, based in Newtownabbey, Northern Ireland. WP Base is the data
        controller for the information described here.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you have a question about this policy or about your information, you
        can email <a href="mailto:hello@wpbase.co.uk">hello@wpbase.co.uk</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>What information is collected</h2>
      <p>
        The amount of information collected depends on how you interact with WP
        Base.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Enquiries and audit requests.</strong> When you complete a
          form on this site, you provide your name, email address, and whatever
          details you choose to include about your website or business. Some
          forms also ask for a phone number or website URL.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email correspondence.</strong> If you email directly, that
          message and your email address are held in the WP Base mailbox.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Care plan customers.</strong> If you subscribe to a plan,
          billing details are collected and processed by Stripe. WP Base does
          not see or store your full card number. Records of invoices and
          subscriptions are kept for accounting purposes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Client site access.</strong> Where WP Base maintains your
          website, this involves access to hosting accounts, WordPress
          administration and related credentials. That access is used only for
          the work you have asked for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Website analytics.</strong> With your consent, analytics and
          advertising cookies record pages viewed, approximate location, device
          and browser type, and how you arrived at the site.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Why it is collected, and the lawful basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>To respond to your enquiry.</strong> Lawful basis: legitimate
          interests, in that you have contacted a business expecting a reply.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To deliver services you have paid for.</strong> Lawful basis:
          performance of a contract.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To keep accounting and tax records.</strong> Lawful basis:
          legal obligation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To measure how the website and any advertising performs.</strong>
          Lawful basis: consent, given through the cookie banner and withdrawable
          at any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>To send occasional updates, where you have asked for them.</strong>
          Lawful basis: consent. Every message includes an unsubscribe link.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Who else handles your information</h2>
      <p>
        WP Base does not sell your information and does not share it for anyone
        else's marketing. A small number of service providers process data on WP
        Base's behalf in order to run the business.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> for website hosting and security.</li>
        <li><strong>Fillout</strong> for enquiry and audit request forms.</li>
        <li><strong>Zoho Mail</strong> for email.</li>
        <li><strong>Stripe</strong> for payments and subscription billing.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google Analytics and Google Tag Manager</strong> for website
          measurement, where you have consented.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>LinkedIn</strong> for advertising and conversion measurement,
          where you have consented.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Some of these providers are based outside the UK. Where that is the
        case, transfers are covered by the UK International Data Transfer
        Agreement, the UK Addendum to the EU Standard Contractual Clauses, or an
        adequacy decision.
      </p>
      <p>
        Information may also be disclosed where there is a legal requirement to
        do so.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        This site sets cookies that are necessary for it to work, and these do
        not require your consent. Analytics and advertising cookies are only set
        after you agree through the cookie banner. You can change or withdraw
        that choice at any time using the cookie settings link in the footer, and
        you can block or delete cookies in your browser settings.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How long information is kept</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Enquiries that do not become work:</strong> up to two years,
          then deleted.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Client records and correspondence:</strong> for the length of
          the working relationship and six years afterwards.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Invoices and financial records:</strong> six years, as
          required by HMRC.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics data:</strong> in line with the retention period set
          in Google Analytics, currently 14 months.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask WP Base to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>confirm what information is held about you, and give you a copy;</li>
        <li>correct anything that is inaccurate or incomplete;</li>
        <li>delete your information, where there is no reason to keep it;</li>
        <li>restrict or object to how it is used;</li>
        <li>transfer it to another provider in a portable format;</li>
        <li>stop sending you marketing, at any time.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Email <a href="mailto:hello@wpbase.co.uk">hello@wpbase.co.uk</a> and you
        will get a response within one month.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are unhappy with how your information has been handled, you can
        complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at
        <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>, by phone on
        0303 123 1113, or by post to Wycliffe House, Water Lane, Wilmslow,
        Cheshire, SK9 5AF.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Accounts are protected with strong unique passwords and two-factor
        authentication where it is available. Client credentials are stored in a
        password manager rather than in email or plain text files. No system is
        completely secure, but reasonable technical and organisational measures
        are in place to protect what is held.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        This policy may be updated as the business or its tools change. The date
        at the top shows when it was last revised.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: var(--reading, 800px);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 6rem 1.5rem 5rem;
  }

  .legal-header {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .legal h1 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .legal-meta {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .legal section {
    margin-bottom: 2.75rem;
  }

  .legal h2 {
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', system-ui, sans-serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .legal p,
  .legal li {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .legal p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .legal ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .legal li {
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .legal a:hover {
    text-decoration-color: var(--accent, #d4ff3a);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .legal {
      padding-top: 4.5rem;
    }
  }
</style>
